adjudication.rationale:
In `addGuests.handler.ts`, the mutation explicitly allows non-organizers to add guests (`isAttendee` check and `!isTeamAdminOrOwner && !isOrganizer && !isAttendee` guard). However, the calendar update is performed using an `EventManager` constructed from `ctx.user` and `getUsersCredentials(ctx.user)`:
```ts
const credentials = await getUsersCredentials(ctx.user);
const eventManager = new EventManager({ ...user, credentials: [...credentials] });
await eventManager.updateCalendarAttendees(evt, booking);
```
`evt.organizer` is derived from `booking.userId`/`organizer`, i.e., the booking organizer, so when an attendee (or other permitted non-organizer) triggers this, the calendar update will run under the wrong user's credentials. This can plausibly fail to update the organizer’s destination calendar event or update the wrong calendar association.
